// callMethod() v1 is capped to natives only, on all three backends
// (notes/expressiveness-roadmap.md item 1). A method backed by a
// user-defined closure is a runtime error even on JVM/CLR, which have no
// technical reason of their own to refuse it - parity with native wins.
class Greeter {
    greet() { return "hi"; }
}
var g = Greeter();
print "before";
callMethod(g, "greet");
